Z||000000||Elenor84||02-25-2001||01:22 PM||||When I try to start my car now I get a grinding noice...I just replaced my starter so I hope its not that...what could it be?  Oil is nice and high...thx!<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||02-25-2001||01:43 PM||||Incorrect starter shim.<BR>Check and install proper shims.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Elenor84||02-25-2001||02:02 PM||||I installed the starter my self about 3 weeks ago...what are shims?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||02-25-2001||02:27 PM||||Shims: A spacer that goes in between parts where alignment or clearance issues are involved or are a concern for proper function.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Elenor84||02-25-2001||05:01 PM||||Alright thank you...I'll check that out tomorrow...	<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Carrolles||02-26-2001||07:48 AM||||The new starter should have come with a couple of shims.  They are long thin metal strips with a hole on one end and a slot on the other.  You use them to set the proper clearance between the starter gear and the flywheel ring gear and they bolt in between the starter and the engine.<P>When the starter gear is engaged you should be able to slip a paper clip between the gears (crude measurement but it works).  This is a bit of a pain to check though.  Try installing a shim and see if it quiets down.  If you did not get shims with the starter and lost yours, any parts store should have a variety pack in the HELP brand of accessories.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Elenor84||02-26-2001||02:12 PM||||Just threw the fiero in the shop today guys...as I was going in I couldn't start the car...all I heard was the starter missing and then winding up...so I know its the starter...it'll be fixed by the end of the day...thx so much guys ofr your help<BR>You all rock!<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||JohnnyK||02-26-2001||02:25 PM||||Unless of course you chewed the flywheel and/or starter to shreds already.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I had the same problem. i just found the shim that fell out when I took my old starter out and reused it.||||reg||1
